.TH CRUNCH-AR 1 "November 2026" "Crunch 0.9.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
crunch-ar \- experimental static archive utility
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B crunch-ar
.RI { r | q | d | t | x }[ cvs ]
.I archive
.RI [ members ...]
.br
.B crunch-ar s
.I archive
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B crunch-ar
creates and modifies regular GNU-format static archives on x86-64 Linux.
It is experimental and is not a complete replacement for GNU ar.
Updates are written to a temporary file beside the archive and replace it
only after a successful write. Archive metadata is deterministic.
.SH OPERATIONS
.TP
.B r
Replace matching members or add new ones.
.TP
.B q
Append members, including duplicate names.
.TP
.B d
Delete one matching member for each supplied name.
.TP
.B t
List members, optionally selecting names.
.TP
.B x
Extract members, optionally selecting names. Names containing path separators
are rejected.
.TP
.B s
Rebuild the archive symbol index.
.SH MODIFIERS
.TP
.B c
Accepted for GNU ar compatibility.
.TP
.B s
Write the archive symbol index. It is also written automatically by
.BR r ,
.B q
and
.BR d .
.TP
.B v
Print member operations or a detailed table of contents.
.SH LIMITATIONS
The symbol index supports ELF64 little-endian x86-64 relocatable objects and
32-bit GNU archive offsets. Non-ELF members are stored without indexed symbols.
Thin archives, BSD extended names, extended ELF symbol indices, and other GNU
ar operations and modifiers are unsupported.
